changed [web_aws_instance]: main.tf:37: aws_instance.web: a document's ids are unique and "web" was taken or reserved, so this is "web_aws_instance" here and aws_instance.web_aws_instance once compiled. An existing state still knows it as aws_instance.web: move it with `terraform state mv aws_instance.web aws_instance.web_aws_instance` before applying, or it is destroyed and created again.
changed [web_aws_eip]: main.tf:58: aws_eip.web: a document's ids are unique and "web" was taken or reserved, so this is "web_aws_eip" here and aws_eip.web_aws_eip once compiled. An existing state still knows it as aws_eip.web: move it with `terraform state mv aws_eip.web aws_eip.web_aws_eip` before applying, or it is destroyed and created again.
not translated: main.tf:83: moved block: a moved block changes what the state records and has no counterpart in a document. Do it once with the tool before Meridian takes over, then it is not needed
not translated: outputs.tf:1: output "address": a document's output has a name and a value, so "description" was left out
not translated: outputs.tf:10: output "instance_ids": a document's output has a name and a value. `sensitive` was left out, so the value is shown in plans and logs unless what it reads is itself marked sensitive
not translated: versions.tf:1: terraform.required_version: the constraint ">= 1.6" on the tool's own version has nowhere to go in a document; pin the terraform binary Meridian runs instead
note [random]: versions.tf:1: required_providers.random: the configuration requires this provider without configuring it, so this resource carries only its source and version and compiles to an empty provider block
